</tgroup></table>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((-3)^2+10=9+10=19\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((-2)^2+10=4+10=14\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((-1)^2+10=1+10=11\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((0)^2+10=0+10=10\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((1)^2+10=1+10=11\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((2)^2+10=4+10=14\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((3)^2+10=9+10=19\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use the table with different values of \(x\) to answer questions a–g for the values of \(x^2-3\). (You may
    also use a spreadsheet tool, if available.)</item>
</list>
