<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)? <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\((-3)^2-3=9-3=6\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((-2)^2-3=4-3=1\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((-1)^2-3=1-3=-2\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)? <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\((0)^2-3=0-3=-3\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-2. (1)2-3=1-3=-2\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((2)^2-3=4-3=1\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)? <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\((3)^2-3=9-3=6\)
  </item>
</list>
