<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac{1}{2}(-3)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 9=\frac{9}{2}=4\frac{1}{2}=4.5\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac{1}{2}(-2)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 4=\frac{4}{2}=2\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac{1}{2}(-1)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 1=\frac{1}{2}=0.5\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac{1}{2}(0)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 0=0\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac{1}{2}(1)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 1=\frac{1}{2}=0.5\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(\frac{1}{2}(2)2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 4=\frac{4}{2}=2\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(\frac{1}{2}(3)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 9=\frac{9}{2}=4\frac{1}{2}=4.5\)
  </item>
</list>
