<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-2(-3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-2(-2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-2(-1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-2(0)^2=-2 \cdot 0=0\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-2(1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-2(2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-2(3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)
  </item>
</list>
